{
 "source": "the dry run's Velocity time limit and its two slots. Each sleep waits (replay) until the run before it holds its slot, and the limit is 3 s rather than 400 ms, so on a loaded host runs a and b still hold both slots when the third arrives; the sleep after them waits until their threads gave the slots back (the answer is sent just before)",
 "properties": {
  "velocityTemplateExecutionTimeout": "3000"
 },
